{"parentUuid":"af3835ea-d233-4893-bc18-59e5466a40f0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cer8wDfubsb9rhhKcVwVY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fine — and it turns out the SDK bought you nothing. Every lever is a CLI flag on your installed 2.1.263:\n\n- `--system-prompt` / `--system-prompt-file` — **full replacement**, not just append. I was wrong about that last message; the CLI has both.\n- `--setting-sources` — same isolation as the SDK option, so no user/project/local leakage.\n- `--mcp-config` + `--strict-mcp-config` — only your server, ambient MCP config ignored.\n- `--allowed-tools` / `--disallowed-tools`\n- `--session-id` — you assign the UUID, so you know the transcript path before the process starts.\n- `--permission-prompt-tool` for the hands-free approval story later.\n\nRoughly:\n\n```bash\nCLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/abs/path/to/voicectl/.claude \\\nclaude \\\n  --system-prompt-file ./prompts/controller.md \\\n  --setting-sources '' \\\n  --mcp-config ./mcp.json --strict-mcp-config \\\n  --allowed-tools 'mcp__ctl__*' \\\n  --session-id \"$CTL_SESSION\"\n```\n\nCheck the exact argument shapes against `claude --help` — I verified the flag names exist in the bundle, not their arities.\n\n## The one thing that actually changes: output\n\nWithout the SDK you have no structured event stream, and scraping the pane with `capture-pane` is a losing game — ANSI, redraws, spinners, wrapping.\n\n**Make `speak(text)` an MCP tool and let it be the only way the controller produces audio.** This is better than the SDK's message stream, not a fallback for it:\n\n- You get exactly the text meant for your ears. No filtering thinking, tool chatter, or status lines out of a transcript.\n- The model can call it *early* in a turn, before it finishes reading a session. That recovers most of the streaming latency you lost — it says \"checking\" and then speaks the answer, instead of you waiting on a completed turn.\n- It composes with the draft tools. `stage_draft` returns the readback text; the controller speaks it. Deterministic content, model-controlled timing.\n\nThe failure mode is the model forgetting to call it, so add a **`Stop` hook in the isolated config dir** that tails the controller's own JSONL (`$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects/<slug>/<session-id>.jsonl` — and you know that path because you set `--session-id`) and speaks the assistant turn if `speak` wasn't called. Silence becomes impossible, and the hook lives in the controller's config so it never touches your real setup.\n\nThat also means you're writing exactly one JSONL tailer and using it twice: once to read target sessions, once as the controller's own safety net.\n\n## Tool surface, final\n\n```\nlist_sessions()\nread_session(session, since?)\nstage_draft(session, text) / amend_draft / discard_draft\nsend_draft(session)          # only thing that writes to a session\nspeak(text)\n```\n\nSix tools, `--allowed-tools 'mcp__ctl__*'`, nothing else. No Bash, no Read, no Edit — a controller that can edit files will eventually decide to do the work itself.\n\nBuild order: `list_sessions` + `read_session` + `speak` first, driven by typing at the controller. That's enough to answer \"what's it doing\" and \"tell me more about that part,\" which is the half of your use case that proves the loop. Drafting and `send_draft` second.\n\nReady to create the directory and scaffold when you are — just tell me where."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":154885,"output_tokens":2015,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":846},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2015,"cache_read_input_tokens":154885,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cer8wBsGD2FgYG9TrHD7b","type":"assistant","uuid":"c0da0863-7391-4e9f-a132-7b018d37ef5e","timestamp":"2026-09-08T14:34:36.135Z","effort":"high","session_id":"1768614c-2d2a-40b0-9f02-a9aaf381ef7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/bmf/code/happy","sessionId":"1768614c-2d2a-40b0-9f02-a9aaf381ef7f","version":"2.1.263","gitBranch":"happy-agent-context-bap"}
